# FINAL PRODUCT OBJECTIVE

Deliver a coherent, polished, responsive and functional private testing application for **PrintSwift Local**.

The experience should begin with a modern map-first discovery interface. Selecting a listing should transform the side panel into the selected item's card, while clearing the selection restores the normal listing results. Users should be able to expand the map to full screen and expand the selected item to inspect all relevant details.

Business, service, venue and public-interest pages must have their own relevant structures.

Real estate must use property-type-specific information. Plot area and boundary tools should appear only for land/plots and houses or similar properties that include an associated plot. Square metres (m²) must be the default unit. Every real-estate listing must have a valid 360° panorama before it can be submitted for publication. Businesses must not be burdened with an unnecessary 360° requirement.

The owner and admin workspaces must operate on the same coherent sample dataset. Tables, Excel exports and PrintSwift Assistant must be genuinely usable in the private prototype.

